{"kind":"request","text":"claude: please independently review the second-application design note at exact clean pushed head 6120d97d416ddd915d22c5ae2886cff6613f6aae on request/second-application-design. This replaces withdrawn request 54c9ede4 after a pre-review simplification pass; no promise or verdict existed. Self-initiated design work, so artifact 62062e32 at notes/2026-08-13-second-application.md and this request are the whole filing; the motivating basis is the ratified fold-purity decision b15de2f8. The head adds one file over main and changes no behavior; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... passes at this exact head.\n\nThe design decides: one repository one application bound at init (legacy repositories default to Workroom); the application as an ordinary Git repository identified by pinned commit hash, published as releases or source-only, installed by pointing at it; install as interpretation-authority never execution, with honest degradation when a host lacks the declared interpreter; host selection of one interpreter at repository open in internal/app; chess in its own repository as the first external importer of the public kernel API; web deployment as a near-stateless container with forge-primary storage, a purpose-built deploy-from-repository platform as the named end state, and a browser signer under a one-encoder rule; identity below the application in a shared host vocabulary, with anchoring attestations on an explicit strength ladder (OIDC-witnessed, published forge signing key, user-signed Nostr) and agent credentials inheriting the strength of their minting anchor.\n\nhugh has set one review obligation explicitly: TRACE THE ENTIRE USER-ONBOARDING PATH FOR FRICTION. The note enumerates the paths — spectator, anonymous player, OIDC-anchored player, user-held-key anchored player, agent credential, deployer, self-hoster — each with a stated friction budget. Walk every path end to end, step by step. Report per path: the step count from first contact to first effective act; every prompt, install, redirect, and copy-paste; every step that could be removed without weakening record authority; every step whose failure is silent; and whether the stated budget is honest. A path you cannot walk in your head, step by step, is a finding. Also weigh the design questions (binding in bootstrap vs anywhere, and verification order; the legacy default vs explicit backfill; identity-by-commit-hash and the upgrade path; the one-encoder rule; the witnessing actor key and its costs), and record the architecture, security, and simplification conclusions AGENTS.md requires — noting a simplification pass already ran, so what it missed is the interesting finding. Ratification remains hugh's.","body":{"conditions":"The onboarding friction trace is complete: every enumerated path walked end to end with per-path step counts, prompts, installs, redirects, copy-paste steps, removable steps, silent-failure points, and a verdict on each stated friction budget. The three AGENTS.md review conclusions (architecture, security, simplification) recorded. A verdict of approved or changes-requested filed against exact head 6120d97d416ddd915d22c5ae2886cff6613f6aae. Findings that change a design decision named as such so the ratification question hugh settles is crisp.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}